questions lists every name -f takes in place of a path, with the file it resolves to.

-f NAME looks in the nearest .onesie/questions at or above the working directory, then in questions under the config dir that holds profiles.json, and tries NAME.yaml, NAME.yml and NAME.json. Last it takes the starter sets built into onesie, which list as built in. A name in more than one place lists only the first, which is the one -f uses, so a saved copy of a built in set wins. A name with two files in one directory is listed once per file and marked as a clash, which -f refuses.

Usage:
  onesie questions [flags]

Examples:
  mkdir -p .onesie/questions
  onesie --ask urgent='is this urgent' --print-questions > .onesie/questions/triage.yaml
  onesie questions

Flags:
  -h, --help            help for questions
  -o, --output string   table, json or auto, which means table

Global Flags:
      --profile string    The profile a run uses, from profiles.json in the config dir. Overrides ONESIE_PROFILE and ONESIE_PROVIDER. Otherwise the default profile runs, which onesie profile use sets.
      --provider string   Run on this provider without a profile: typesafe, openrouter, berget, levanto or cloudflare. Overrides ONESIE_PROVIDER and the default profile. Refused beside --profile or ONESIE_PROFILE.
